('111.27.b.5.A',4,'Which is true about similar figures?','["Corresponding sides are proportional", "All sides are equal", "All areas are equal", "They must be the same size"]'::jsonb,0,'Similar figures have proportional sides.','original'),
('111.27.b.5.A',4,'Rectangles with sides 2×3 and 4×6 are...','["not similar", "similar", "congruent", "equal in area"]'::jsonb,1,'Both ratios 2:3 and 4:6 are equal.','original'),
('111.27.b.5.A',4,'Rectangles with sides 2×3 and 4×5 are...','["similar", "congruent", "not similar", "equal in area"]'::jsonb,2,'2/3 does not equal 4/5.','original'),
('111.27.b.5.B',2,'π is the ratio of a circle''s circumference to its...','["chord", "radius", "area", "diameter"]'::jsonb,3,'π = C ÷ d.','original'),
('111.27.b.5.B',3,'A circle has circumference 31.4 cm and diameter 10 cm. What is 31.4 ÷ 10?','["3.14", "0.314", "31.4", "10"]'::jsonb,0,'That ratio is about π.','original'),
('111.27.b.5.B',3,'Which is the closest approximation of π?','["2.14", "3.14", "4.13", "1.14"]'::jsonb,1,'π ≈ 3.14.','original'),
('111.27.b.5.B',4,'Any circle''s circumference divided by its diameter is always...','["exactly 3", "the radius", "the same number, π", "different for each circle"]'::jsonb,2,'That constant ratio is π.','original'),
('111.27.b.5.C',3,'A scale drawing uses 1 inch = 5 feet. A room is 4 inches wide in the drawing. How wide is the real room?','["1.25 feet", "4 feet", "9 feet", "20 feet"]'::jsonb,3,'4 × 5 = 20.','original'),
('111.27.b.5.C',3,'On a map, 2 cm represents 10 km. How far apart are two towns that are 7 cm apart on the map?','["35 km", "3.5 km", "14 km", "70 km"]'::jsonb,0,'Each cm is 5 km: 7 × 5 = 35.','original'),
('111.27.b.5.C',4,'A model car is 1/24 the size of a real car. The real car is 192 inches long. How long is the model?','["216 inches", "8 inches", "168 inches", "4608 inches"]'::jsonb,1,'192 ÷ 24 = 8.','original'),
('111.27.b.5.C',4,'A photo 4 in × 6 in is enlarged to be 10 in wide. How tall is the enlargement?','["14 in", "12 in", "15 in", "16 in"]'::jsonb,2,'Scale factor 10/4 = 2.5; 6 × 2.5 = 15.','original'),
('111.27.b.5.C',4,'A 6 ft tall person casts a 4 ft shadow. At the same time a tree casts a 20 ft shadow. How tall is the tree?','["80 ft", "24 ft", "13 ft", "30 ft"]'::jsonb,3,'6/4 = x/20 gives x = 30.','original'),
('111.27.b.6.A',3,'A coin is flipped once and a die is rolled once. How many outcomes are in the sample space?','["12", "8", "7", "6"]'::jsonb,0,'2 × 6 = 12.','original'),
('111.27.b.6.A',3,'Two coins are flipped. Which list shows the sample space?','["HH, TT", "HH, HT, TH, TT", "HH, HT, TT", "H, T"]'::jsonb,1,'There are four equally likely outcomes.','original'),
